    id: String.raw`i-ShhCNkX`,
    title: String.raw`Miles to Go`,
    alt: String.raw`Photographic artwork © Wayne Heim`,
    description: String.raw`Wayne Heim’s painterly Western fine art photograph, featuring two riders and a young horse trekking through open country under golden light. This evocative image captures not just the journey, but the rite of passage—where green horses, seasoned cowboys, and the wild West itself shape one another. Every sun-warmed detail, from weathered tack to shifting shadows, is rendered in Heim’s distinctive painterly style.
Discover more Western Cowboy Portraits
 and painterly Western fine art at K4 Studios. © Wayne Heim`,
    story: String.raw`Another crossing.
Closing in.
Daylight writes her closing hymn.

Miles to go
to reach the end.

God be willing,
this path less followed…
leads us back
to home again.`,
    notes: String.raw`This scene calls back to the golden age of Western painters—think Charles Russell’s trail stories, or the mentorship found in Frederic Remington’s lesser-known works. Here, Heim’s painterly process turns a moment of guidance and learning into a work of enduring art. The colt’s youthful energy, set against the steady presence of the riders, becomes a metaphor for the passing down of knowledge and the untamed promise of the West. Every brushstroke and highlight feels deliberate, pulling the viewer into the rhythm of the journey and the quiet legacy of life on the trail.`,
    src: String.raw`https://photos.smugmug.com/Other/Photo-Shoots/South-Dakota/Artist-Ride-2025/i-ShhCNkX/0/KSxzs9TCd6hb98VK9VdQ966LgjM9vHKjpTMv5Pt6G/XL/_WHO5919-909-XL.jpg`,
    srcXL: String.raw`https://photos.smugmug.com/Other/Photo-Shoots/South-Dakota/Artist-Ride-2025/i-ShhCNkX/0/KSxzs9TCd6hb98VK9VdQ966LgjM9vHKjpTMv5Pt6G/XL/_WHO5919-909-XL.jpg`,
