    id: String.raw`i-DwVBJb3`,
    title: String.raw`Dead to Rights`,
    alt: String.raw`Cowboy Art:  Dead to Rights`,
    description: String.raw`Dead to Rights. Old bearded cowboy stands over the body of his latest victim. Embrace the spirit of the Old West with Wayne Heim’s captivating cowboy art and western photographs. Each piece of his fine art photography, infused with a unique painterly photography style, captures the raw emotion and timeless beauty of the frontier. Bring the essence of the Wild West into your space with stunning western art that immortalizes the cowboy spirit. © Wayne Heim`,
    story: String.raw`Dead to Rights. Old bearded cowboy stands over the body of his latest victim. Embrace the spirit of the Old West with Wayne Heim’s captivating cowboy art and western photographs. Each piece of his fine art photography, infused with a unique painterly photography style, captures the raw emotion and timeless beauty of the frontier. Bring the essence of the Wild West into your space with stunning western art that immortalizes the cowboy spirit. © Wayne Heim`,
    notes: String.raw`This portrait asserts authority through structure rather than violence. The low vantage point and upward gaze establish dominance without requiring action, placing the figure in command of both space and consequence.

The weight of the coat, the settled grip, and the stillness of posture suggest finality rather than threat. This is not the moment of conflict, but the aftermath—where power is measured by what no longer needs to be done. Within Western imagery, the work distinguishes itself by treating force as resolved history, not spectacle. The figure stands as a record of consequence, aligning the piece more closely with narrative painting than performative genre portraiture.`,
    src: String.raw`https://photos.smugmug.com/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color/i-DwVBJb3/2/L3r5bTvGFn74qBHMqQZKPRHv5CdtnvWpfPxHpXD6m/XL/Old%20West%20Cowboy%20Portrait%20_O1H0568-Edit-Edit-XL.jpg`,
