    id: String.raw`i-sLL3pQG`,
    title: String.raw`Cold Inevitability`,
    alt: String.raw`Western figure standing at the edge of a cliff, caught between decision and hesitation in painterly fine art photography.`,
    description: String.raw`A painterly Western fine art photograph by Wayne Heim capturing a solitary figure at the edge—resolve and hesitation sharing the same breath. The minimal composition and fractured light highlight longing, regret, and the stubborn way hope interrupts even the clearest mission. © Wayne Heim`,
    story: String.raw`The ground ends. All that weight behind him—choices, debts, her—caught in the quiet. He came ready, or so he thought. No more almost.

Steps forward, then a flicker—off to the side. A break in the light. Is that something, or just hope, working its old trick again? Can’t tell. Doesn’t matter. He hesitates.

Funny thing about cliffs: sometimes the only thing sharper than the edge is the doubt that finds you just before you jump.`,
    notes: String.raw`This piece distills the Western pause before consequence—where resolve and doubt are twins. Heim’s restraint leaves the story open, letting viewers decide if hesitation is grace, weakness, or simply proof of being alive.`,
    src: String.raw`https://photos.smugmug.com/Other/Photo-Shoots/South-Dakota/Artist-Ride-2025/i-sLL3pQG/0/MxPH5sMTSPhHbH7pqpmd9pRZqVgvFBW6Lwz4nRG7z/XL/_WHO2916-1148-XL.jpg`,
    srcXL: String.raw`https://photos.smugmug.com/Other/Photo-Shoots/South-Dakota/Artist-Ride-2025/i-sLL3pQG/0/MxPH5sMTSPhHbH7pqpmd9pRZqVgvFBW6Lwz4nRG7z/XL/_WHO2916-1148-XL.jpg`,
