    id: String.raw`i-wdF6Hw3`,
    title: String.raw`Last Light on the Cook Wagon`,
    alt: String.raw`Cowboy cook standing beside a chuck wagon at sunset holding a tin cup, painterly Western portrait.`,
    description: String.raw`A painterly Western portrait capturing a rare moment of calm at the end of a long day on the trail. Standing beside a chuck wagon at sunset, the cowboy cook holds a tin cup as warm firelight illuminates his weathered face and apron. Wayne Heim’s cinematic, textured approach blends illustration-inspired tones with fine art photography, creating a nostalgic tableau rich in atmosphere and narrative. Ideal for collectors of Western fine art, Americana wall decor, and story-driven frontier imagery.`,
    story: String.raw`The trail was long, the miles unforgiving, but the day always ended here—beside the wagon, where the coffee was hot and the stories were warmer. As the sun bled out behind the horizon, he lingered in the glow, cup in hand, letting the quiet settle over him like a worn blanket. 

Tomorrow the riders would saddle up before dawn. Tonight, he allowed himself this moment—watching the firelight dance across the prairie, knowing that even the hardest trails need a heartbeat of rest.`,
    notes: String.raw`Heim’s mastery of cinematic natural light is on full display here. The interplay of fire glow and fading daylight recalls the tonal discipline of Frederic Remington’s nocturnes while maintaining the softness and narrative subtlety of pictorialist photography. Compositionally, the frame leads the eye from the illuminated foreground into the cooling horizon, emphasizing the emotional rhythm of work and rest on the American frontier. This piece carries the quiet dignity of a life lived in service to others—a timeless cowboy archetype reimagined through Heim’s painterly, story-driven lens.`,
    src: String.raw`https://photos.smugmug.com/Other/Photo-Shoots/South-Dakota/Artist-Ride-2025/i-wdF6Hw3/1/LksDQhMZLgf7TRVdTB26w6Gbc4ZP9LbpDGG6fTfQB/XL/_WHO7929-Edit-XL.jpg`,
